.TH mbpy_3dtiles 1 "12 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP \- Create an executable shellscript which will make the
standard 3D products of a survey (GLBs, OGC 3D Tiles tilesets and X3DOM and CesiumJS pages)
with mbgrd2gltf, mbmesh and mbglb2tiles.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP [\fB\-I\fP\fIsurveydir\fP] [\fB\-O\fP\fIroot\fP]
[\fB\-\-subdir\fP\fIname\fP] [\fB\-\-grid\fP\fIname\fP] [\fB\-\-datalist\fP\fIname\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-geoorigin=\fP\fIlon,lat,elev\fP] [\fB\-\-lift\fP\fImeters\fP] [\fB\-\-reference\-subdir\fP\fIname\fP]
[\fB\-L\fP\fImeters\fP] [\fB\-\-threads\fP\fIn\fP] [\fB\-\-no\-label\-chunks\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-x3dom\-url\fP\fIurl\fP] [\fB\-\-no\-cesium\-html\fP] [\fB\-\-cesium\-url\fP\fIurl\fP] [\fB\-\-no\-survey\-page\fP]
[\fB\-\-mbgrd2gltf\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP] [\fB\-\-mbmesh\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP]
[\fB\-\-mbglb2tiles\-args=\fP\fIargs\fP]
.br
[\fB\-\-force\fP] [\fB\-X\fP] [\fB\-V\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbpy_3dtiles\fP is a macro that writes a shellscript, \fIroot\fP.sh
(default 3dtiles.sh, in the survey directory), and with \fB\-X\fP runs it.
It is meant to be run in a survey directory that has a subdirectory for each
kind of data, by default \fBmultibeam\fP and \fBlidar\fP, each with a grid,
\fBZTopo.grd\fP, and a datalist of processed swath data, \fBdatalistp.mb\-1\fP.
A subdirectory, or a file in it, that is not there is left out. The commands,
in the order that they run, with paths relative to the survey directory:
.br
1. \fBmbgrd2gltf\fP \-\-input \fIdir\fP/ZTopo.grd \-\-html \-\-cesium\-html \-\-geoorigin \-\-output \fIdir\fP/ZTopo
.br
2. \fBmbmesh\fP \-\-input \fIdir\fP/datalistp.mb\-1 \-\-html \-\-cesium\-html \-\-threads \-\-geoorigin \-L
\-\-raw\-mesh\-glb \-\-pointcloud\-glb \-\-track\-glb \-\-label\-chunks \-\-output \fIdir\fP/mbmesh_output
.br
3. \fBmbglb2tiles\fP of \fIdir\fP/ZTopo.glb (to \fIdir\fP/ZTopo_tileset) and of
\fIdir\fP/mbmesh_output/mesh.glb, each with \-\-html \-\-cesium\-html \-\-x3dom\-url \-\-lift
.br
4. \fBmbmesh\fP \-\-input . \-\-html \-\-cesium\-html \-\-geoorigin \-\-x3dom\-url, the survey pages, mbmesh_survey.html and mbmesh_survey_cesium.html.
.PP
There is one GeoOrigin for a survey, which every program gets so that the models line up,
and one lift, which every tileset gets. Without \fB\-\-geoorigin\fP the GeoOrigin is the center
of the grid of the reference subdirectory (\fBmultibeam\fP) and the mean of its heights, read with \fBgmt grdinfo\fP; without
\fB\-\-lift\fP the lift puts the lowest point of that grid 10 m above the
ellipsoid, to a meter. The other subdirectories, the lidar for example, get the same ones.
\fBZTopo.grd\fP is a standard product of a survey, which this macro does not make: a subdirectory
that has a datalist and no grid, or a grid and no datalist, gets a warning on standard error
that says what will not be made, whatever \fB\-V\fP says.
.PP
A full run takes hours, so the shellscript runs a command only if it has something to do: if one of its
outputs (the GLBs, the tilesets and the pages that it writes) is missing or older, by modification time, than
one of its inputs. The inputs are the grid, for \fBmbgrd2gltf\fP; the datalist and every swath file that it names, the
processed files too, for \fBmbmesh\fP; the GLB, for \fBmbglb2tiles\fP; and the outputs of all the other commands, for the
survey pages. The commands run in order, so what an earlier command makes again makes what depends on it stale. The shellscript
checks when it runs, not when it is written. A command that is not run is reported as up to date. A change of an
option cannot be seen this way: use \fB\-\-force\fP, or \fBFORCE=1\fP in the environment of a shellscript made without it.
.PP
The pages and their logs need a web server: from the
survey directory, \fBpython3 \-m http.server\fP.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-I\fIsurveydir\fP, \-\-input
The survey directory [the current directory].
.TP
.B \-O\fIroot\fP, \-\-output
The shellscript is \fIroot\fP.sh [3dtiles].
.TP
.B \-\-subdir \fIname\fP
A subdirectory to process; can be repeated [multibeam, lidar].
.TP
.B \-\-grid \fIname\fP, \-\-datalist \fIname\fP
The names of the grid and the datalist [ZTopo.grd, datalistp.mb\-1].
.TP
.B \-\-geoorigin=\fIlon,lat,elev\fP
The GeoOrigin, with the height above the ellipsoid. A value that begins with a
minus has to be attached with an equals sign.
.TP
.B \-\-lift \fImeters\fP
How far the tilesets are lifted above the ellipsoid.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Make every product again, whatever the modification times say.
.TP
.B \-\-reference\-subdir \fIname\fP
The subdirectory whose grid sets the GeoOrigin and the lift of the whole survey [multibeam].
.TP
.B \-L\fImeters\fP, \-\-lod
The smallest feature size of \fBmbmesh\fP [0.1].
.TP
.B \-\-threads \fIn\fP, \-\-no\-label\-chunks
Chunks that \fBmbmesh\fP reconstructs at once [8]; leave the chunk outlines out of the pages.
.TP
.B \-\-x3dom\-url \fIurl\fP
The X3DOM script of the pages of \fBmbglb2tiles\fP and the survey page
[./x3dom\-full.js]; it is relative to each page.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cesium\-html
Leave out \fB\-\-cesium\-html\fP, the pages for CesiumJS, from every command.
.TP
.B \-\-cesium\-url \fIurl\fP
The directory of the CesiumJS build that the pages for CesiumJS load, given to each command as \fB\-\-cesium\-url\fP
[the default of each program, release 1.114 from Cesium's web site].
.TP
.B \-\-no\-survey\-page
Leave out the survey page.
.TP
.B \-\-mbgrd2gltf\-args=\fIargs\fP, \-\-mbmesh\-args=\fIargs\fP, \-\-mbglb2tiles\-args=\fIargs\fP
More options for the programs, as one quoted string.
.TP
.B \-X
Run the shellscript.
.TP
.B \-V
Print how the GeoOrigin and the lift were set and the commands, each marked "will run" or "skipped" with the reason, as the
modification times are now: an output that is missing, an input that is newer than an output, or an input that an earlier
command that will run makes again; with \fB\-\-force\fP every command will run. The shellscript looks at the files again each time
it runs, so this is what it would do if it were run now.

